<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tanaro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tanaro is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, rising in the Ligurian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> and flowing past Alba, Asti and Alessandria before joining the Po. About 276 km long, it is the main right-bank tributary of the upper Po. Medieval communes such as Asti and Alessandria grew along its valley, which carried routes between the Po plain and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liguria">Liguria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tanaro.jpg" alt="Tanaro" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Neq00 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fiume_Tanaro_al_tramonto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
